# ============================================================================
# coconut_gazebo.param -- Gazebo-only deltas, applied AFTER coconut_quadplane.param
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SITL is started with `-f quadplane --model JSON`, so quadplane.parm supplies
# the base defaults, coconut_quadplane.param the airframe, and this file only
# what differs because the physics now come from Gazebo
# (models/coconut_quadplane, generated by gen_sdf.py).
# ============================================================================

# The Gazebo plugin provides no airspeed sensor: fly on the synthetic estimate.
ARSPD_TYPE        0
ARSPD_USE         0

# Real elevon outputs: the Gazebo model de-mixes nothing, each elevon is its
# own joint, so 77/78 stay as on the real aircraft (no SITL aileron override).
SERVO1_FUNCTION   77
SERVO2_FUNCTION   78
SERVO1_REVERSED   0
SERVO2_REVERSED   0

# Plugin maps 1000..2000 us onto every channel.
SERVO3_MIN        1000
SERVO3_MAX        2000
SERVO3_TRIM       1000

# Fixed-wing roll: quadplane.parm's gains weave +-20 deg on these full-span
# elevons (aero/control_authority.py: ~10x a normal plane's roll power).
# Starting point pending AUTOTUNE. Halved when MIXING_GAIN went 0.5 -> 1.0
# (same roll loop gain, double the available throw).
RLL_RATE_P        0.04
RLL_RATE_I        0.06
RLL_RATE_D        0.0
RLL_RATE_FF       0.225

# Lift rotors must stay OFF in cruise. With cruise 12 / assist 9 m/s the
# synthetic airspeed (~10 m/s) kept dipping under Q_ASSIST_SPEED and the lift
# motors re-engaged every few seconds. Cruise a bit faster, keep assist as a
# genuine near-stall safety net (Vs ~7.5 m/s, aero/RESULTS.md).
# Printed build is 1.84 kg (airframe/BUILD_NOTES.md): wing loading 6.1 kg/m^2,
# Vs ~8.9 m/s in 35 C air.
AIRSPEED_CRUISE   15
AIRSPEED_MIN      12
Q_ASSIST_SPEED    9
# 5 m/s wind (fw_wind5): downwind turns still dipped to 8.9 m/s and assist
# cycled 6x per sweep. Stall ~9.4 m/s level, ~10.4 m/s at 35 deg bank, so
# cruise 15 / min 12 keeps the margin in wind.

# Point the nose (and wing) along the direction of travel during the VTOL
# tree-to-tree hops instead of crabbing sideways like a multicopter.
# QuadPlane only auto-yaws to the waypoint on long post-transition approaches;
# on short hops it holds heading + weathervane. Weathervaning turns the nose
# into the relative airflow, which during a hop comes from the direction of
# travel -- and the fins then help instead of fighting the yaw controller.
Q_WVANE_ENABLE    1
Q_WVANE_GAIN      4        # max: gain 2 still trailed the hop direction by 35-80 deg
Q_WVANE_SPD_MAX   0
Q_WVANE_VELZ_MAX  0
Q_WVANE_HGT_MIN   0

# Arm without RC input (fully autonomous demo, no transmitter in the loop).
ARMING_RUDDER     0
THR_FAILSAFE      0

# Light, slow wing: 45 deg banks (n=1.41) used up the elevator margin at
# 12 m/s and ended in a spiral dive (fw_calm recorded run). 35 deg: n=1.22.
ROLL_LIMIT_DEG 35

# Pitch authority: elevons on a 0.16 m arm behind the CG (the stab is fixed).
# With MIXING_GAIN 0.5 the elevator got half the elevon throw and the pitch
# loop could not stop a nose drop in a 35 deg bank (fw_wind5: spiral dive to
# the ground). 1.0 gives the full throw to pitch.
MIXING_GAIN 1.0
